#: ../../../install.md:5
msgid "Installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:8
msgid ""
"The [Quickstart](#quickstart) section just below provides the fastest way to "
"install PyGMT, whereas the following sections afterward provide more "
"detailed, step-by-step instructions for users who may have different setups "
"or want to install the latest development version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:13
msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:15
msgid ""
"The fastest way to install PyGMT is with the [conda](https://docs.conda.io/"
"projects/conda/en/latest/user-guide/index.html) package manager, which takes "
"care of setting up a virtual environment, as well as the installation of GMT "
"and all the dependencies PyGMT depends on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:20
msgid "conda create --name pygmt --channel conda-forge pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:24
msgid "To activate the virtual environment, you can do:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:26 ../../../install.md:107
msgid "conda activate pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:30
msgid ""
"After this, check that everything works by running the following in a Python "
"interpreter (e.g., in a Jupyter notebook):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:35 ../../../install.md:172
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"pygmt.show_versions()"
msgstr ""

