#: ../../../install.md:42
msgid ""
"You are now ready to make your first figure! Start by looking at our [Intro]"
"(intro/index.rst), [Tutorials](tutorials/index.rst), and [Gallery](gallery/"
"index.rst). Good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:46
msgid "Which Python?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:48
msgid "PyGMT is tested to run on Python {{ requires.python }}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:50
msgid ""
"We recommend using the [Miniforge](https://github.com/conda-forge/miniforge) "
"Python distribution to ensure you have all dependencies installed. "
"Installing Miniforge does not require administrative rights to your computer "
"and doesn't interfere with any other Python installations on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:55
msgid "Which GMT?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:57
msgid ""
"PyGMT requires Generic Mapping Tools (GMT) {{ requires.gmt }} since there "
"are many changes being made to GMT itself in response to the development of "
"PyGMT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:60
msgid ""
"Compiled conda packages of GMT for Linux, macOS and Windows are provided "
"through [conda-forge](https://anaconda.org/conda-forge/gmt). Advanced users "
"can also [build GMT from source](https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/gmt/"
"blob/master/BUILDING.md) instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:65
msgid "We recommend following the instructions further on to install GMT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:67
msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:69
msgid "PyGMT depends on GMT and the following Python libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:71
msgid ""
"**Required**: [NumPy](https://numpy.org/), [pandas](https://pandas.pydata."
"org/), [xarray](https://xarray.pydata.org/), [packaging](https://packaging."
"pypa.io/en/stable/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:76
msgid ""
"**Optional**: [IPython](https://ipython.org/), [GeoPandas](https://geopandas."
"org/), [contextily](https://contextily.readthedocs.io/), [rioxarray](https://"
"corteva.github.io/rioxarray/), [PyArrow](https://arrow.apache.org/docs/"
"python/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:83
msgid "For detailed version requirements, see [](minversions.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:85
msgid "Installing GMT and other dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:87
msgid ""
"Before installing PyGMT, we must install GMT itself along with the other "
"dependencies. The easiest way to do this is via the `conda` package manager. "
"We recommend working in an isolated [virtual environment](https://conda.io/"
"projects/conda/en/latest/user-guide/tasks/manage-environments.html) to avoid "
"issues with conflicting versions of dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:93
msgid ""
"First, we must configure conda to get packages from the [conda-forge channel]"
"(https://conda-forge.org/):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:94
msgid "conda config --prepend channels conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:98
msgid ""
"Now we can create a new virtual environment with Python and all our "
"dependencies installed (we'll call it `pygmt` but feel free to change it to "
"whatever you want):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:101
msgid ""
"conda create --name pygmt python=3.14 numpy pandas xarray packaging gmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:105
msgid ""
"Activate the environment by running the following (**do not forget this step!"
"**):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:111
msgid ""
"From now on, all commands will take place inside the virtual environment "
"called `pygmt` and won't affect your default `base` installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:115
msgid ""
"You can also enable more PyGMT functionalities by installing PyGMT's "
"optional dependencies in the environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:117
msgid "conda install contextily geopandas ipython pyarrow-core rioxarray\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:122
msgid "Installing PyGMT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:124
msgid ""
"Now that you have GMT installed and your virtual environment activated, you "
"can install PyGMT using any of the following methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:127
msgid "Using conda (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:129
msgid ""
"This installs the latest stable release of PyGMT from [conda-forge](https://"
"anaconda.org/conda-forge/pygmt):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:131
msgid "conda install pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:135
msgid ""
"This upgrades the installed PyGMT version to be the latest stable release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:137
msgid "conda update pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:141
msgid "Using pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:143
msgid ""
"This installs the latest stable release from [PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/"
"pygmt):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:144
msgid "python -m pip install pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:149
msgid ""
"You can also run `python -m pip install pygmt[all]` to install PyGMT with "
"all of its optional dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:153
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can install the latest development version from [TestPyPI]"
"(https://test.pypi.org/project/pygmt):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:155
msgid ""
"python -m pip install --pre --extra-index-url https://test.pypi.org/simple/ "
"pygmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:159
msgid ""
"To upgrade the installed stable release or development version to be the "
"latest one, just add `--upgrade` to the corresponding command above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:162
msgid ""
"Any of the above methods (conda/pip) should allow you to use the PyGMT "
"package from Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:165
msgid "Testing your install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:167
msgid ""
"To ensure that PyGMT and its dependencies are installed correctly, run the "
"following in your Python interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:181
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(projection=\"R7c\", region=[0, 360, -90, 90], frame=True)\n"
"fig.coast(land=\"tan\", water=\"lightblue\")\n"
"fig.text(position=\"MC\", text=\"PyGMT\", font=\"40p,AvantGarde-Book,red\", "
"transparency=75)\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:181
msgid "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:187
msgid ""
"You should see a global map with land and water masses colored in tan and "
"lightblue respectively. On top, there should be the semi-transparent text "
"\"PyGMT\". If the semi-transparency does not show up, there is probably an "
"incompatibility between your GMT and Ghostscript versions. For details, "
"please run `pygmt.show_versions()` and see [Not working transparency](#not-"
"working-transparency)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:193
msgid "Common installation issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:195
msgid ""
"If you have any issues with the installation, please check out the following "
"common problems and solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:198
msgid "\"Error loading GMT shared library at ...\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:200
msgid ""
"Sometimes, PyGMT will be unable to find the correct version of the GMT "
"shared library (`libgmt`). This can happen if you have multiple versions of "
"GMT installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:203
msgid ""
"You can tell PyGMT exactly where to look for `libgmt` by setting the "
"environment variable {term}`GMT_LIBRARY_PATH` to the directory where `libgmt."
"so`, `libgmt.dylib` or `gmt.dll` can be found on Linux, macOS or Windows, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:207
msgid ""
"For Linux/macOS, add the following line to your shell configuration file "
"(usually `~/.bashrc` for Bash on Linux and `~/.zshrc` for Zsh on macOS):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:209
msgid "export GMT_LIBRARY_PATH=$HOME/miniforge3/envs/pygmt/lib\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:213
msgid ""
"For Windows, add the environment variable {term}`GMT_LIBRARY_PATH` following "
"these [instructions](https://www.wikihow.com/Create-an-Environment-Variable-"
"in-Windows-10) and set its value to a path like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:216
msgid "C:\\Users\\USERNAME\\Miniforge3\\envs\\pygmt\\Library\\bin\\\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:220
msgid "`ModuleNotFoundError` in Jupyter notebook environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:222
msgid ""
"If you can successfully import PyGMT in a Python interpreter or IPython, but "
"get a `ModuleNotFoundError` when importing PyGMT in Jupyter, you may need to "
"activate your `pygmt` virtual environment (using `conda activate pygmt`) and "
"install a `pygmt` kernel following the commands below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:226
msgid ""
"python -m ipykernel install --user --name pygmt  # install virtual "
"environment properly\n"
"jupyter kernelspec list --json\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:231
msgid ""
"After that, you need to restart Jupyter, open your notebook, select the "
"`pygmt` kernel and then import pygmt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:234
msgid "Not working transparency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:236
msgid ""
"It is known that some combinations of GMT and Ghostscript versions cause "
"issues, especially regarding transparency. If the transparency doesn't work "
"in your figures, please check your GMT and Ghostscript versions (you can run "
"`pygmt.show_versions()`). We recommend:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:241
msgid "Ghostscript 9.53-9.56 for GMT 6.4.0 (or below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:242
msgid "Ghostscript 10.03-10.07 for GMT 6.5.0-6.7.0"
msgstr ""
